  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\n$P_{14-16}$ : Paragraph for Questions Nos. 14 to 16 A fixed thermally conducting cylinder has a radius $R$ and height $L_0$. The cylinder is open at its bottom and has a small hole at its top. A piston of mass $M$ is held at a distance $L$ from the top surface as shown in the figure. The atmospheric pressure is $p_0$.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/4uUwDqNsXDagR3met7Ief3ZxT31gi025zIfyrEsgmZk.original.fullsize.png\"><br><strong>Question:</strong>\nThe piston is now pulled out slowly and held at a distance $2 L$ from the top. The pressure in the cylinder between its top and the piston will then be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "1xf2B",
      "text": "\n$p_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "qSQgH",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{p_0}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MhO4t",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{p_0}{2}+\\frac{M g}{\\pi R^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Q2ESc",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{p_0}{2}-\\frac{M g}{\\pi R^2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since it is open from top, pressure will be $p_0$. $\\therefore$ Option (a) is correct.",
